        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "bert.pdf:p2:region:2",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 2,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "sentence (Kiros et al., 2015), or denoising autoencoder derived objectives (Hill et al., 2016)."
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "bert.pdf:p2:region:2",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "ELMo and its predecessor (Peters et al., 2017,"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "bert.pdf:p2:region:2",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 2,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "2018a) generalize traditional word embedding research along a different dimension. They extract"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "bert.pdf:p2:region:2",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 4,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "right-to-left language model. The contextual representation of each token is the concatenation of the left-to-right and right-to-left representations. When integrating contextual w"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "bert.pdf:p2:region:2",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 4,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "contextual representations through a task to predict a single word from both left and right context using LSTMs. Similar to ELMo, their model is feature-based and not deeply bidire"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "bert.pdf:p2:region:2",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "et al. (2018) shows that the cloze task can be used"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "bert.pdf:p2:region:2",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "As with the feature-based approaches, the first"
        },
        {
          "kind": "list",
          "regionId": "bert.pdf:p2:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 3,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "• BERT advances the state of the art for eleven NLP tasks. The code and pre-trained models are available at https://github.com/"
        },
        {
          "kind": "list-item",
          "regionId": "bert.pdf:p2:region:0",
          "parent": "bert.pdf:p2:block:list:0",
          "lines": 3,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "• BERT advances the state of the art for eleven NLP tasks. The code and pre-trained models are available at https://github.com/"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "bert.pdf:p2:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 3,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "like Radford et al. (2018), which uses unidirectional language models for pre-training, BERT uses masked language models to enable pre"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "bert.pdf:p2:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 3,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "is also in contrast to Peters et al. (2018a), which uses a shallow concatenation of independently trained left-to-right and right-to-left LMs."
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "bert.pdf:p2:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "There is a long history of pre-training general lan"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "bert.pdf:p2:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "most widely-used approaches in this section."
        },
        {
          "kind": "unknown",
          "regionId": "bert.pdf:p2:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "• We demonstrate the importance of bidirectional"
        },
        {
          "kind": "unknown",
          "regionId": "bert.pdf:p2:region:2",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "els."
        }
      ]
    },
