        {
          "kind": "caption",
          "regionId": "bert.pdf:p5:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "Figure 2: BERT input representation. The input embeddings are the sum of the token embeddings, the segmenta"
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "regionId": "bert.pdf:p5:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "tion embeddings and the position embeddings."
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "regionId": "bert.pdf:p5:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "shuffled sentence-level corpus such as the Billion"
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "regionId": "bert.pdf:p5:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "extract long contiguous sequences."
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "regionId": "bert.pdf:p5:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "lows BERT to model many downstream tasks—"
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "regionId": "bert.pdf:p5:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "whether they involve single text or text pairs—by"
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "regionId": "bert.pdf:p5:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "swapping out the appropriate inputs and outputs."
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "regionId": "bert.pdf:p5:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "For applications involving text pairs, a common"
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "regionId": "bert.pdf:p5:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "pattern is to independently encode text pairs be"
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "regionId": "bert.pdf:p5:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "fore applying bidirectional cross attention, such"
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "regionId": "bert.pdf:p5:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "as Parikh et al. (2016); Seo et al. (2017). BERT"
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "regionId": "bert.pdf:p5:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "these two stages, as encoding a concatenated text"
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "regionId": "bert.pdf:p5:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "rectional cross attention between two sentences."
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "bert.pdf:p5:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "are analogous to (1) sentence pairs in paraphras"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "bert.pdf:p5:region:2",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "tailment or sentiment analysis."
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "bert.pdf:p5:region:2",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "In this section, we present BERT fine-tuning re"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "bert.pdf:p5:region:2",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 6,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "The General Language Understanding Evaluation (GLUE) benchmark (Wang et al., 2018a) is a collection of diverse natural language understanding tasks. Detailed descriptions of GLUE d"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "bert.pdf:p5:region:2",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 2,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "sequence (for single sentence or sentence pairs) as described in Section 3, and use the final hid"
        }
      ]
