          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "connection and element-wise addition. We adopt the sec"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "resnet.pdf:p3:region:3",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "The shortcut connections in Eqn.(1) introduce neither ex"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "resnet.pdf:p3:region:3",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 3,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "Plain Network. Our plain baselines (Fig. 3, middle) are mainly inspired by the philosophy of VGG nets [41] (Fig. 3, left). The convolutional layers mostly have 3×3 filters and"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "resnet.pdf:p3:region:3",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "feature map size, the layers have the same number of fil"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "resnet.pdf:p3:region:3",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "convolutional layers that have a stride of 2. The network"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "resnet.pdf:p3:region:3",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "layer baseline has 3.6 billion FLOPs (multiply-adds), which"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "resnet.pdf:p3:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "explicitly let these layers approximate a residual function"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "resnet.pdf:p3:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "F(x)+x. Although both forms should be able to asymptot"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "resnet.pdf:p3:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "problem. If the optimal function is closer to an identity"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "resnet.pdf:p3:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 3,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "by experiments (Fig. 7) that the learned residual functions in general have small responses, suggesting that identity mappings provide reasonable preconditioning."
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "resnet.pdf:p3:region:0",
          "parent": null,
