      "headings": 1,
      "unknown": 2,
      "previews": [
        {
          "kind": "list",
          "regionId": "tracemonkey.pdf:p2:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 2,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "This paper makes the following contributions:\n• We explain an algorithm for dynamically forming trace trees to"
        },
        {
          "kind": "list-item",
          "regionId": "tracemonkey.pdf:p2:region:0",
          "parent": "tracemonkey.pdf:p2:block:list:0",
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "• We explain an algorithm for dynamically forming trace trees to"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "tracemonkey.pdf:p2:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 3,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "a na¨ıve implementation, inner loops would become hot first, and the VM would start tracing there. When the inner loop exits, the VM would detect that a different branch was taken."
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "tracemonkey.pdf:p2:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 2,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "on ever tracing outer loops. We solve the nested loop problem by recording"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "tracemonkey.pdf:p2:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 2,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "loop, but then it starts a new trace at the outer loop header. When the outer loop reaches the inner loop header, the system tries to call"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "tracemonkey.pdf:p2:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 3,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "the outer trace as normal. In this way, our system can trace any number of loops nested to any depth without causing excessive tail duplication."
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "tracemonkey.pdf:p2:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "We implemented these techniques for an existing JavaScript in"
        },
        {
          "kind": "list",
          "regionId": "tracemonkey.pdf:p2:region:2",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "2. Overview: Example Tracing Run"
        },
        {
          "kind": "list-item",
          "regionId": "tracemonkey.pdf:p2:region:2",
          "parent": "tracemonkey.pdf:p2:block:list:1",
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "2. Overview: Example Tracing Run"
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "regionId": "tracemonkey.pdf:p2:region:2",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "how TraceMonkey executes an example program. The example"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "tracemonkey.pdf:p2:region:2",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "Record Enter"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "tracemonkey.pdf:p2:region:2",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "LIR Trace Compiled Trace"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "tracemonkey.pdf:p2:region:2",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "LIR Trace Compiled Trace"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "tracemonkey.pdf:p2:region:2",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "existing trace"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "tracemonkey.pdf:p2:region:2",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "Compiled Trace"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "tracemonkey.pdf:p2:region:2",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "code interpreter. Every loop back edge is a potential trace point."
        },
        {
          "kind": "unknown",
          "regionId": "tracemonkey.pdf:p2:region:2",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "loop/exit"
        },
        {
          "kind": "unknown",
          "regionId": null,
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "finish at nested trace loop header loop edge with"
        }
      ]
