        {
          "kind": "caption",
          "regionId": "tracemonkey.pdf:p3:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "Figure 3. LIR snippet for sample program. This is the LIR recorded for line 5 of the sample program in Figure 1. The LIR encodes"
        },
        {
          "kind": "caption",
          "regionId": "tracemonkey.pdf:p3:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "Figure 4. x86 snippet for sample program. This is the x86 code compiled from the LIR snippet in Figure 3. Most LIR instructions compile"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "tracemonkey.pdf:p3:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "v0 := ld state[748] // load primes from the trace activation record"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "tracemonkey.pdf:p3:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "st sp[0], v0 // store primes to interpreter stack"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "tracemonkey.pdf:p3:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 2,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "v1 := ld state[764] // load k from the trace activation record\nv2 := i2f(v1) // convert k from int to double"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "tracemonkey.pdf:p3:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 2,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "st sp[8], v1 // store k to interpreter stack\nst sp[16], 0 // store false to interpreter stack"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "tracemonkey.pdf:p3:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 3,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "v3 := ld v0[4] // load class word for primes\nv4 := and v3, -4 // mask out object class tag for primes\nv5 := eq v4, Array // test whether primes is an array"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "tracemonkey.pdf:p3:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "xf v5 // side exit if v5 is false"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "tracemonkey.pdf:p3:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 2,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "v6 := js_Array_set(v0, v2, false) // call function to set array element\nv7 := eq v6, 0 // test return value from call"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "tracemonkey.pdf:p3:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 1,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "xt v7 // side exit if js_Array_set returns false."
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "tracemonkey.pdf:p3:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 2,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "the semantics in SSA form using temporary variables. The LIR also encodes all the stores that the interpreter would do to its data stack.\nSometimes these stores can be optimized aw"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "tracemonkey.pdf:p3:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 22,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "mov edx, ebx(748) // load primes from the trace activation record\nmov edi(0), edx // (*) store primes to interpreter stack\nmov esi, ebx(764) // load k from the trace activation rec"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "regionId": "tracemonkey.pdf:p3:region:0",
          "parent": null,
          "lines": 3,
          "mapped": true,
          "text": "to a single x86 instruction. Instructions marked with (*) would be omitted by an idealized compiler that knew that none of the side exits\nwould ever be taken. The 17 instructions g"
        }
      ]
